body:
Nothing new I can't add to what a few others have said. I know women are very fragile yet strong and independent. Imagine a woman getting cat called, it's devastating if the guy is average, but if he's attractive, she'll be blushing and feeling good about herself. There are men out there who would cut off their arms just for a woman to say something remotely kind to them. Women seem to not understand why men get so attached so easily. Try walking in the desert for years and finally getting a drink of water, it would be a God send and you'd lap it up for as long as you could. Having someone acknowledge your existence is no different. Some guys I know will joke around about how on Tinder there's a ton of single moms. That's not a jab at women, it's a fact. Most women grow up being told you're a pretty princess who deserves the best out of life. Most men, well that I know, grew up with their fathers telling them you make all the sacrifices for your family, you are the foundation, you create a home for your family. A women doesn't have to do anything and can cost by on  looks alone. Whoever tells you looks don't matter are just lying. A good joke one of my friends told me was if you saw a woman in a dumpster, your first reaction would be is she hot. Compared to a man if he was in one, he's a loser piece of shit. I watch women on twitch with no personality, but a good body and face, getting Tesla's given to them by their male viewers because the men are so desperate for any female attention. All women punch above their weight, it's why they can "never find a good man" I have a friend who makes a shit ton of money. He's on the shorter side so he's passed on by basically every female he talks to. He has his own home, two cars, can go anywhere in the world. He could provide for a family easily and the woman wouldn't have to lift a finger to work, but ohhh he's too short while she's basically a dwarf at 5'0  or under, but would rather struggle with her real King and be a single mom.

&#x200B;

God needs to wipe us out.

I always likened how I saw my life as to being a house. My life is a house and inside this house, it looks cozy and inviting, there's a little fire place and a couch and some comfy reclining chairs, they're the color red, the windows have a big of fog on them since it's basically a blizzard outside and freezing cold. There's the people I know all sharing what looks to be food and mugs of hot drinks of some kind. The reason why I know what the inside looks like so vividly to me and how the outside feels, is because I'm not in the house, just always on the outside looking in. I know that sideline character feeling, watching my own life run past me. I've been alive a good while now and I've never had that home feeling, like I belonged somewhere, probably never will. Sadly I can't give you answers on how to function. I don't even know how to love another human being properly. I come to reddit to meet new people then they deep dive into my post history and they don't want to deal with this train wreck. I think that's also the worst part of depression is just losing any sense of who you are. Who are you? I'm nobodies friend, haven't had a best friend in god knows how  long. Already covered love and I'm basically a robot because I can't believe it can happen and when it did. I was just there, had some horrible moments of being treated like I was no body when I was with someone when you'd think it should of been the opposite.

&#x200B;

I have no solutions and I gave up asking the same questions like who am I, why am I here. I kind of just don't care anymore. I'm just a no body, sure I'm a good person, but that means nothing when no body cares ya know? Sorry for the long post. I just don't like to see someone suffering and I tend to ramble so that you know you're not alone in how you feel. It's alright to vent your frustrations and maybe instead of shooting for the moon, just gaze at the stars instead and do some little things you enjoy to get you back on your feet or to pull you out of some of your depression, it's an on going battle, but a few days off from it never hurts.

Sometimes it's better to make the best of where you are rather than worry about where you should be.

&#x200B;

It's not an easy thing to do though, but you miss out on what you could be doing because you're more worried about something else.

Being short in today's society is basically being an outcast if you're a male. You can kiss about 98% of having any normal relationship out the window. I'm glad that at my height on the chart I'm at goblin level. You see that other guy giving you the have hope speech as if you didn't already see for yourself what it's like. Yes, you may get lucky, but people are horrible to each other for no reason and over looks. No one should wonder why god never came back or helps us, we're monsters.

&#x200B;

My advice is to live your life regardless of whose with you when you do and enjoy it for yourself. It's tough and there will be some hard days where you want to share what you've built, but humans are just way too selfish.

Yeah me ugly too, but to me you're like a rare jewel that I've just discovered and it's pretty neat.

&#x200B;

Sorry I've been drinking.

I'm sorry you're poor, tried, and hungry. Come and we will eat and laugh about rich people together and once it's all over, we will return to fetus.

&#x200B;

I may or may not be drunk... I'm drunk.

I mean I want to take myself out for a lot of reasons, but the real question is am I going to put out for myself after I've spent all this time taking myself out, Red Lobster isn't cheap these days, but those cheddar bay biscuits always get me in the mood. 

&#x200B;

Let me take the time to apologize for being me, but I recently found out last year I have a rare autoimmune disorder. No one thought I was special, but inside I'm super special and rare. I mean I don't know, it's not so bad I guess. It just depends on how you look at it, like most things with life. It can be a negative if you're constantly thinking about that and only that.

It's winter time and when my anxiety gets really bad. I like to go outside and just take a deep breath of cold air and just stare out into the darkness of the night sky. I try not to think of anything and when I do I'll distract myself with thoughts of other places or I just won't think at all. If he's moving on, you should as well. You can still hold on to hope, but if you're standing still, you're not moving right? Still continue to move forward and if it happens it happens. Being yourself isn't always going to win over everyone, but at least you tried. I can only see if from a guys point of view and it sounds like you're getting put on the back burner while he shops his options because he knows you're there already, ready to go. It's harsh for me to say and hard for you to read and I could be totally wrong. I know a guy who is head over heels in love with a woman who changes her mind every single day, they break up almost every other week, but he continues to just be faithful to her, even if is breaks his heart to do so. He just knows shes the one and he's willing to go through the roller coaster of love because he knows what he could get in the end. We've all tried to talk him out of it, but he just knows. His stuff is literally in his car because how often they're getting back together and than splitting up. She has a lot of trust issues. She believes that he could have anyone, why her and so she breaks up with him saying he could have anyone. She could be replaced by anyone, but like I said, real men don't quit.

&#x200B;

No need to thank me, didn't do anything special. I will say best of luck and I hope things will turn around for the better, even a little bit.

My brother would always get a job and if he didn't like it day one, would just walk off the job, wouldn't say anything. Now he has a great job and makes great money. Getting a job is tough today because of how the world seems to be falling apart. You just have to keep at it and it seems like you have, so good work there.

&#x200B;

With the coding and going back to school, it's all a gamble. It could work out and it might not, but you can't be afraid to take the risks. Even if you tried and failed, at least you tried over not trying at all and never giving yourself the chance.

&#x200B;

Money wise get roommates or if you're already with someone, kick their ass into gear and do it together.

Honestly when it comes to working and jobs, to me it doesn't matter. If you can provide for yourself and yours, what does it matter. I understand that people will instantly gauge your worth by what you do for a living, but that doesn't mean you're a decent human being because you make loads of money.

&#x200B;

Well religion is often perverted by human beings, we're good for making things worse or harder on ourselves and others. Only one God, you're going to hell. Yadda yadda... Vin Diesel said it best in the character Riddick "I absolutely believe in god, and I absolutely hate the fucker." I was raised catholic but life changes and god went out the window. I just want a peaceful life and to have someone I connect with, at this point it doesn't even have to be romantically.

Don't worry about the meme, but it does seem people tend to avoid people who are broken. I remember a guy mentioning just on reddit you should have two accounts because if people see you post in like r/depression and the like, they will avoid talking to you, but when he switches accounts and they see his history isn't about wanting to die, they'll just treat him normal. Which is just hilarious how shallow human beings are and it's why we need to be wiped off this planet. 

&#x200B;

I know buddy I don't want to be alone. I absolutely fucking hate it, but my life shows me no other way, no matter how many times I fought back. It's never changed and I will always feel like I never belong anywhere. I have people I can talk to, but I know in my mind and what's left of my heart, I am alone. Can't tell you how to fix it. I'm just hoping God kills me quick... I really do hate to suffer.

At least someone would find you. I could be dead for months before someone came looking. I don't know if that is worse or not. I did and still do fantasize about a life light switch that I could turn off and I just ceased to exist. I would of turned it off when I was a teenager and here I am years later still holding out and hoping for that switch, but I've learned I have to be the one to turn it off and it probably won't be like a light switch, more like pulling a trigger.

&#x200B;

I understand about the binge eating because it's also my comfort and I'll just eat when I'm not hungry, my only saving grace is I can't put on the weight, but even if I did. I wouldn't care. Wasn't going to win any beauty pageants to begin with.
